id:                     E6402
trigger_tool:           target-shell|toybox|consumer|mktemp
phase:                  W3-consumer|target-runtime
error_signature:        mktemp: need XXXXXX: Not supported
severity:               2
category:               ohos,toolchain,shell,consumer,evidence
match_keywords:         toybox mktemp, XXXXXX suffix, temporary config, target shell, predictable PID filename, TMPDIR
title:                  OHOS toybox mktemp templates must end with XXXXXX

root_cause:             The OpenHarmony target toybox mktemp parser requires the six X placeholders to be the final template characters and rejects a literal suffix after them. A host GNU mktemp check may accept name.XXXXXX.conf, while the target fails before launching the consumer. This is a target-tool capability difference, not a package or application failure.
affected_scope:        Shell consumers and task-owned target wrappers that create unique temporary files on OpenHarmony toybox images.
verification_cmd:      Run the production target shell with a template ending in XXXXXX, record the returned path, execute the consumer, and verify uniqueness plus zero task-owned temporary files after EXIT cleanup.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           target-compatible-mktemp-template
rec_description:        Use an opaque mktemp template whose final six characters are XXXXXX, keep the parent directory task-owned, and remove the returned file in an EXIT trap. Reject predictable PID names and any host-only assumption about suffix support.
rec_command:            mktemp "$TMPDIR/consumer-config.XXXXXX"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               production consumer shell template

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      fixed-name-with-lock
fallback_description:   A fixed name with an exclusive create can be used only when the target contract proves atomic no-replace creation and the path is task-private; it is not a substitute for mktemp when concurrent consumers share a directory.
fallback_command:       use only under an explicit no-replace contract
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:           task-specific wrapper

forbid_1_pattern:       append a literal extension after XXXXXX|accept host GNU mktemp as target proof
forbid_1_reason:        Toybox rejects the template before the application runs, and host utility semantics differ from the target image.
forbid_1_consequence:   The consumer flow fails despite a successful build and can be misclassified as an application regression.
forbid_2_pattern:       use predictable $$ or a shared fixed filename
forbid_2_reason:        Concurrent or repeated flows can collide and the filename does not provide a safe uniqueness contract.
forbid_2_consequence:   Inputs can be overwritten or stale data can be consumed, invalidating target evidence.

principles:             P005,P010,P013
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

